    "site_desc": "This tower is located in the Barrow Environmental Observatory (BEO), in Barrow, Alaska, on native land set-aside for research.  The Barrow-BEO site has well-developed high-centre, flat-centre and low-centre polygons. The vegetaiton vegetation on polygon high centres consisted of Polytrichum moss and lichen-dominated communities with few vascular plants. Polygon rims and flat centres were dominated by a mixture of graminoids, including Eriophorum russeolum (sedge), Poa arctica (grass) and Luzula arctica (rush), with Dicranum mosses, liverworts and frequent lichens. More details are in Davidson et al. (2016).",
